# --- /proyectos/ : retired Spanish ad-campaign landings -----------------------
# These were never organic pages. Each is a templated Spanish landing with a
# Calendly embed, a WhatsApp CTA and 9 utm_ params, hreflang'd to its /co/ and
# /es/ campaign siblings. Three of the four names do not exist in the
# 31-project Airtable inventory at all, and all four borrow a real project's
# photography (cavarossa-amador x2, buenaventura-resort-cocle,
# allure-punta-pacifica).
#
# GSC, verified live over the full 16-month window on 2026-08-01:
#   - All four detail URLs, in BOTH forms: "URL is unknown to Google",
#     last crawled Never. They were never linked from a sitemap
#     (scripts/build-sitemap.mjs:105 emitted only the hub), so Google has
#     never once seen them.
#   - The /proyectos/ hub is the only URL here with index presence:
#     "Submitted and indexed", last crawled 2026-06-04, 0 clicks /
#     7 impressions / avg position 5.7 over 16 months.
#   - Semrush: 0 referring domains on deep URLs; 93 of 103 point at the root.
#
# 301 rather than 410, which is the opposite of how the /es/, /de/ and /pt/
# trees were handled, and deliberately so. That 410 decision was about
# de-indexing 405 URLs that were indexed and cannibalising their originals.
# Here there is nothing to de-index: Google has never crawled these. The only
# traffic they can still receive is human — an old Meta ad, a WhatsApp
# forward, a bookmark — and for those a working page beats an error page.
#
# Destination is the /projects index, not a specific listing. Sending an
# invented name to a real development would misrepresent the listing; sending
# it to the catalogue just says "that landing is gone, here is what we have."
#
# Note the missing trailing slash on /projects. Next.js 308-normalises
# /projects/ to /projects, so a rule targeting the slashed form costs an extra
# hop on every one of these. Verified in production 2026-08-01.
#
# Both URL forms are covered: the .html form v1 linked internally, and the
# extensionless form each page declared in <link rel="canonical">, og:url and
# schema.org url. Only the .html form was mapped before the 2026-08-01 audit,
# so every canonical URL these pages advertised was 404ing.
